[quote]
[h1]Construction Manager[/h1]
A massive quality of life mod that adds new automations, filters, and map modes, to greatly improve the EU5 construction experience.

[h1]Automation Features[/h1]
[list]
 [*][b]Auto-Build[/b]: Hands-free construction paid from a share of your treasury. Six categories (Food, Core Goods, Roads, Production, Custom and Governors) work down a priority list you set, and all but Governors carry their own budget share.
 [*][b]Lucky Nations[/b]: A game rule that gives Auto-Build to chosen AI countries, including capital moves and governor placement. It grants them no bonuses or cheats, only better construction decisions. Single-player only.
 [*][b]Auto-Expand Enabled Buildings[/b]: When toggled will continue to build new levels of the building when possible. You can toggle it for each building on a per location basis, or enable mass expand for a building, where it will construct as many as possible in all eligible locations. Foreign buildings in other countries' locations are covered too.
 [*][b]Auto-Expand Enabled RGOs[/b]: Adds new RGO levels in locations where auto-expand is toggled on.
 [*][b]Auto-Upgrade All Buildings[/b]: Upgrades obsolete buildings to their next tier across your country, regardless of whether auto-expand is on for that building.
 [*][b]Select Buildings[/b]: Constructs one-per-location buildings (council halls, libraries, market villages, settlement buildings, infrastructure, and more) in the priority order you choose.
 [*][b]Auto-Expand Food in Enabled Locations[/b]: Builds food-producing RGOs and food buildings in the rural locations you switch it on for, picking the highest marginal food output.
 [*][b]Auto-Urbanize[/b]: Upgrades rural settlements to towns, towns to cities, and cities to megalopolises each month. Sub-toggles per tier, plus an RGO ignore list (gold, gems, spices, etc.).
 [*][b]Capital Buildings[/b]: Constructs your capital-only buildings (royal court, supreme court, war college, admiralty, chancery, parliament, etc.) when conditions allow.
 [*][b]Auto-Grant Urban Rights[/b]: Grants enabled urban rights to your towns, cities and megalopolises in priority order.
 [*][b]Building Cleanup[/b]: Once a year, closes production buildings that have stopped making money and reopens them when their industry recovers. A separate toggle destroys them instead where the location has run out of room.
 [*][b]Highly configurable[/b]: Each feature can be enabled or disabled, with many options such as min-control, min-gold, min-discount, etc.
[/list]

[h1]New Filters[/h1]
Custom search filters added to the location and building lists:
[list]
 [*]Tax Base and Wealth (with and without control scaling)
 [*]Building Levels Filled (relative to supported cap)
 [*]Production Efficiency and Building Level
 [*]Food Potential Per RGO Level
 [*]R.G.O. Value
 [*]Number of Locations Per Province
 [*]Attacker Penalty (from terrain)
 [*]Good Migration Candidate (non-city under 30k pops)
 [*]Auto-Expand Enabled / Disabled
 [*]Local Access to Raw Materials Bonus
[/list]

[h1]Map Modes[/h1]
[list]
 [*][b]Breadbaskets[/b]: Highlights locations where auto-food is enabled.
 [*][b]Food Potential Per RGO Level[/b]: Colors locations by natural food potential. Factors in rgo, terrain, vegetation, climate, named static modifiers, water access, and assumed-max bonuses from windmill, farming village, and irrigation systems etc.
 [*][b]Recommended Urban Rights[/b]: Colors each location by which specialization urban right its buildings can best source from local raw materials. Hover a location to see every right ranked, or switch to a single right's own search map to see how it fits.
 [*][b]Recommended Governor Placement[/b]: Scores every owned location by how much proximity a new governor built there would add.
 [*][b]Recommended Capital Location[/b]: Scores every owned location by how well a capital there would spread proximity. Rank the finder modes by proximity, by tax base, or by population.
 [*][b]Proximity Efficiency Impact[/b]: Colors locations by how much their terrain slows proximity, stripes coastal locations by natural harbor suitability, and overlays roads, rivers, and the routes to your capital.
[/list]

[h1]Requirements[/h1]
Requires the [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3692202776]Community Mod Framework[/url].

[h1]Compatibility[/h1]
[list]
 [*]Save-game compatible.
 [*]Not Ironman/Achievement compatible.
 [*]Integrates with [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3601047146]Glorp UI[/url] - Load Glorp UI after/below Construction Manager
 [*]Load after other UI mods that override the location window if you see conflicts.
[/list]

[h1]Change Log[/h1]
See the [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/changelog/$item-id$]Change Notes on the workshop page[/url].

